# Per-package coverage floors (ratchet: only raise, never lower).
#
# The numbers that matter are the ones the gate actually sees: CI runs
# `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...` + coverage-gate.sh on ubuntu with
# the Go toolchain pinned in .tool-versions (1.26.6) — the canonical source for
# the exact patch, duplicated in the setup-go steps of .github/workflows/*.
# Measurements below are that job's own output (PR #146, run 35788434102):
#
#   package            floor   CI actual   margin
#   cmd/ai-team        59.0    59.57       0.57
#   pkg/approval       75.7    76.98       1.28
#   pkg/artifactstore  76.0    77.13       1.13
#   pkg/checks         64.6    71.75       7.15
#   pkg/delivery       66.8    67.16       0.36
#   pkg/evidence       61.9    62.59       0.69
#   pkg/pipeline       73.8    74.78       0.98
#   pkg/safeio         60.0    64.67       4.67
#   pkg/worker         95.0    96.64       1.64
#   overall            60.0    71.56
#
# Margins are deliberately not uniform: each floor sits wherever its package
# was when it was added, and packages added long ago have drifted upward since
# (checks, safeio). A tight margin is normal, not a bug — delivery has run at
# 0.36pp for a long time. In absolute terms cmd/ai-team's 0.57pp is ~7.6
# statements out of 1341, i.e. one new untested subcommand is expected to fail
# the gate. That is what the ratchet is for.
#
# Do NOT set or move a floor from a local measurement. The same profile on
# darwin with Go 1.27.1 reads noticeably differently, and the gap can exceed
# the margin you are trying to leave:
#
#   cmd/ai-team  59.57 CI vs 60.85 local (1.28pp — larger than its own margin)
#   pkg/safeio   64.67 CI vs 72.67 local (8.00pp — platform-specific code)
#   pkg/pipeline 74.78 CI vs 76.40 local (1.62pp)
#
# Instrumented statement counts differ between Go releases, and build-tagged
# files (safeio, process) change what exists at all per platform. Take the
# number from a CI run of the PR that improves coverage, then subtract a small
# margin. Raising a floor after a real improvement is expected; lowering one is
# rejected by review.
PKG_APPROVAL_FLOOR=75.7
PKG_ARTIFACTSTORE_FLOOR=76.0
PKG_CHECKS_FLOOR=64.6
PKG_CMD_AI_TEAM_FLOOR=59.0
PKG_DELIVERY_FLOOR=66.8
PKG_EVIDENCE_FLOOR=61.9
PKG_PIPELINE_FLOOR=73.8
PKG_SAFEIO_FLOOR=60.0
PKG_WORKER_FLOOR=95.0
